# M2: open the letter, format a selection from the Character menu, change a paragraph's alignment, type over text in overtype
# mode, undo, and save the result as RTF. F8 starts extending the selection (DOSBox's AUTOTYPE cannot hold Shift).
@copy letter.rtf
@open LETTER.RTF
f8 right right right right right    # select "Quill" in the title
f10 right right down down enter     # Character > Italic
esc
down down down                      # into the paragraph of mixed formats
home f8 right right right right right right right
f10 right right down enter          # Character > Bold
f10 right right down down down enter  # Character > Underline
esc
insert x y insert                   # overtype two letters, then insert mode again
f10 right right right down down enter  # Paragraph > Right
f10 right down enter                # Edit > Redo (nothing to redo)
f10 right enter                     # Edit > Undo (the alignment)
f10 down down down enter            # File > Save As...
o u t period r t f enter
f10 down down down down enter       # File > Exit
